Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - relaxed thread checks (LightingLuminol)

Owner decision 2026-10-22 "Tiru penuh LightingLuminol". Adapted from LightingLuminol (GPL-3.0, Bacteriawa, revision 72d51c4d, paper patch 0002 "Base Dirty Patches"), where every TickThread.ensureTickThread body is commented out unconditionally: here all eight overloads keep their check and ask guards/ThreadChecks.refuse before logging and throwing (aurora.bridge.thread-checks: relaxed by default while aurora.bridge.mode admits plugins, bridged, enforced). ReferenceList and IteratorSafeOrderedReferenceSet lock only while checks are relaxed (static final, folded away otherwise; LightingLuminol synchronized every method); CraftWorld#generateTree and CraftBlock#applyBoneMeal take the chunk's own region data through WorldDataAccess leases; CraftWorld#isChunkGenerated lets the global tick take the synchronous branch while relaxed. CraftServer#getCurrentTick and CraftPlayer#teleport0 need no change here: RegionizedServer.getCurrentTick (MC 0078) and OwnedTeleport.joinAsync carry those parts of the port. A relaxed server is unsafe and unqualified.

